												<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: center;"> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">厨力是第一生产力</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">im&nbsp;not&nbsp;proud&nbsp;of&nbsp;that</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"><img src="http://czyesperanza.wdfiles.com/local--files/pictures/imnotproudofthat.png" alt="imnotproudofthat.png" class="image" /></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">...</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">我突然get到了把作者页当沙盒的好处（？</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div id="wiki-tabview-8f43cf4344c1e071f152f17cf6c08411" class="yui-navset"> <ul class="yui-nav"> <li class="selected"><a href="javascript:;"><em>cone</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>David Rosen</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>SY</em></a></li> </ul> <div class="yui-content"> <div id="wiki-tab-0-0"> <p>地址：<a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/cone">http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/cone</a></p> <hr /> <div class="blockquote"> <p>投票并不能帮到作者。但讨论和批评可以。我在此立誓我将给我差评的每篇文章留下评论（但愿大部分我好评的文章也是如此）。</p> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p>我的理论在此：<br /> <a class="newpage" href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/abolish-the-no-vote-downvote-your-friends-and-other-scp-crit">Abolish The No Vote, Downvote Your Friends, and Other Musings</a> by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rjb-r" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1229263&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607498379" alt="RJB_R" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1229263)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rjb-r" >RJB_R</a></span></p> </div> <p>若你也同意，请在评分后留下讨论和批评来帮助作者。</p> <hr /> <p>你能在这一页的底部找到一系列我为什么可能不喜欢你的作品的理由。</p> <hr /> <p>如果你读过我的一篇文章，感觉有什么话要说，请留下评论！正面的、负面的或者两者之间的，我很乐意知道我的写作让你感觉到/想到了什么。</p> </div> <h1><span>CSS主题</span></h1> <p style="text-align: center;">定制的主题，用以给任何页面泼上视觉风格。</p> <h1><span>版式</span></h1> <p style="text-align: center;">模块化工具，用以为文章添加功能。</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong>我投差评的常见原因</strong></p> <p>我的规则是：只要在你的页面源代码里，我就能据此投票。</p> <p>一般来说我没有看到就差评的东西，但有很多东西会让我以负面的态度看待你写的文章。这些是描述我个人观点的指南——它们并不是硬道理，而且它们<strong>绝对</strong>不<em>决定</em>我的观点。I don't really have any instant-downvote triggers, but there's a bunch of things that'll make me see your article in a negative light. These are guidelines that describe my opinions - they are not hard rules, and they <strong>definitely</strong> do not <em>define</em> my opinions.</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong>给大多数文章的指南</strong></p> <p><strong>Poor/lazy formatting:</strong> This probably applies to a good 70% of articles on the site, but if your article is just a page of text, I'm already looking at it in a negative light. If you couldn't take the time to make your page visually interesting, why should I take the time to read it? An image is a great way to break the monotony and get me invested without even having to make me read anything.</p> <p><strong>Caveat:</strong> Your formatting should match the content. A short, simple article should have simple formatting. A longer, more elaborate article can get away with a bit more 'just because I want to' formatting. Don't wear a top hat and a t-shirt.</p> <p><strong>Excluding people:</strong> The majority of the site's userbase is from the US, so when I see an article that assumes that I'm also in the US, as a UK resident, I immediately feel ostracised. For example, if you say &quot;SCP-XXXX is located in North Carolina&quot; without specifying &quot;North Carolina, US&quot;, you're expecting that the person accessing this SCP document is in the US, and by extension the Foundation is US-only, and therefore as a UK reader, I don't count. Make your locations international and we're good.</p> <p>Try not to exclude anyone, even unintentionally.</p> <p><strong>Lack of visual description:</strong> if you're telling me about something - be it an object, an action, a location, or literally anything - <em>please please please</em> describe it in detail. Visual description is the single most important thing to me when it comes to enjoying your article: I personally have to be able to see it in my mind to understand it properly. If you don't describe it, I'll assume things; and when you break those assumptions (which you will, because you don't know what they are), I get confused.</p> <p>It's simple but easy to miss things - if your character walks into a coffee shop, I may assume that the cashier is on the right, and then get confused when you say your character talks to the cashier on the left. When you describe the room, specify that the cashier is on the left, and we're good.</p> <p><strong>Not making me feel something:</strong> there's a lot of very well-written articles out there that are just dull. You can tell an elegant, beautiful story, but if I don't come away from that having felt something or having had my opinion changed, the chance of getting an upvote is very slim. If I feel like my time has been wasted reading a series of words rather than a compelling story, there's a big chance I'll downvote.</p> <p><strong>A rating module at the end of the article:</strong> I firmly believe that ratings are meaningless as a measure of quality. So, by sticking another rating module at the end of your article, you're telling me not only that you disagree, but also that you don't trust me to remember to vote. If votes are so important to you, maybe you'll enjoy another.</p> <p><strong>Losing my interest:</strong> If I find myself not wanting to continue an article, I am not one of those people who thinks &quot;well, I didn't read the whole thing, so I have no right to vote.&quot; I will.</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong>给SCP的指南</strong></p> <p><strong>Big headers telling me about a clearance level:</strong> Clearance levels are <em>very rarely</em> important to your SCP's narrative, and when you open with a big image that tells me I need level 4 clearance or whatever, my mindset immediately switches from &quot;open to experiencing an interesting SCP&quot; to pessimist mode. 99.9% of all SCPs have a clearance restriction, why does your SCP's clearance level need special attention? Use your big header to tell me about <em>literally</em> anything else - <a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/scp-3211">something I need to know immediately</a>, <a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/taboo">important containment procedures that affect me as a reader</a>, or use it to <a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/scp-3448">give context to your narrative</a>.</p> <p><strong>SCP is a common object:</strong> If I could find the item that your SCP is based on in my house, you're on track for a downvote. If I feel <em>at all</em> that the origin of your SCP is &quot;what could I make anomalous?&quot; then your downvote is pretty much guaranteed. Equally, if you're telling me about an anomalous object but you're not telling about its origin, then that's a big weight on the downvote scale.</p> <p>On the flipside, if your SCP is something unusual - like a concept, or a location, or something abstract, then I'm all ears.</p> <p><strong>The word &quot;will&quot;:</strong> Compulsion effects for the sake of them are lazy writing. SCP-XXXX will do this, the subject will then do this, then X happens, then the SCP will do this. You've already lost my interest.</p> <p><strong>Testing testing testing:</strong> the Foundation contains. We're not Aperture Science - once you've done enough tests to establish the most effective way to contain something, <em>stop</em>.</p> <p><strong>Redaction:</strong> I explained my opinion better <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-7159089/your-unpopular-scp-opinions#post-3940816">here</a>, but the gist is don't redact anything unless you've clearly explained (or will clearly explain, later in the article) why it's being redacted. Redacted names of people and places is meaningless (just pick a name/a random place!), and redaction as a substitute for content (&quot;SCP-XXXX then proceeded to [redacted]&quot;) can be an instant downvote.</p> <p><strong>Spooky notes at the end:</strong> There are <em>so, so many</em> articles that conclude with <em>oooo a spooky note</em> or a corrupted-text collapsible or something. Please just fuck off. Come up with something more original.</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong>给001提案的指南</strong></p> <p><strong>无论如何我都可能会差评它：</strong>001提案数目的膨胀，尤其是有些做作想写不止一篇，已经贬值了这个曾经对我来说价值非凡的格式。因此，我对001的标准高得不正常，基本上什么都是差评。让我震惊。任何一个我给出去的好评都是无比反复无常的——如果我读完了然后好评了，我可能会在一个月后回来，然后发现我其实没有被惊艳到，我就会取消好评。 Inflation in 001 proposal numbers, especially with some authors making more than one proposal, has cheapened the once-valuable meaning of the format for me. As a result, my standards are so ridiculously high for 001s that a downvote is basically guaranteed. Amaze me. Any upvotes that I do give out are extremely volatile - if I read it and upvote, then I come back a month later and find that I'm not amazed any more, that upvote disappears.</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong>给搞笑文章的指南</strong></p> <p>对于搞笑文章，其他所有指南都可以无视，只需要重视一件事：</p> <p><strong>它不好笑：</strong>如果我笑了，我就给好评，没有笑，就差评。就是这样。如果我还想说什么深刻的发言的话，我就会留下评论。</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong>给中心页的指南</strong></p> <p><strong>没有解释中心页的用途：</strong>要是我读下来，你的中心页没有让我很好地知道我要写什么来给它做出贡献，你就会得到差评。要不然就是好评。 If I read your hub and I don't have a good idea of what I would need to write to contribute to it, you get a downvote. Otherwise you get an upvote.</p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-1" style="display:none"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <h5><span>机密评估文件 - 3级以上监督员_亲启</span></h5> </div> <div style="background: url(http://kaktuskontainer.wdfiles.com/local--files/rogetcox/Rosencomputers.png) center top no-repeat ; float: left; width: 400px; padding: 1px 15px; margin: 10px 10px 10px 10px; background-color: #fff; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.2);"> <p>Often described as &quot;inconsequential at best&quot;, there is little reason to regard David Rosen at all. Assigned job since 2012 has been to perform user-level Information Technology Support at Site-19. Competency level is debatable, Rosen is not believed to be proficient with any technologies he is certified in. However, this has not been proven and given his perfect attendance record there is no urgent need to replace him.</p> <p>Effectiveness has been uneven. Although machines and devices sent directly to his office are repaired within hours, logs on the Technical Support Request Line often go unheeded. While this may appear to be highly unprofessional, many of the requests to the Technical Support Request Line violate Foundation protocols and, as such, are technically not counted against Rosen for the purposes of his performance reviews. This has played a large part in his continued employment.</p> <p>Rosen is believed to live out of his office, which has been evaluated as one of the filthiest on record for any personnel in the history of the SCP Foundation. Every inch of floor space is covered by various PC parts dating back to the early 1970's.</p> <p>It is required to wear a dust mask before entering the office. The combination of body odor and lithium grease odors has been considered for use as a scent-based deterrent.</p> <p>Rosen is haunted by the memory of his predecessor. System Analyst Patrick Gephart disappeared mysteriously on July 29th, 2011. Since then, Rosen has filed no less than 412 reports indicating he believes Gephart is stalking him or otherwise attempting to undermine him in his Technical Research position.</p> <p>While Rosen has not been able to provide proof of any physical encounters with Gephart, it is notable that no evidence has been found that Gephart exited Site-19 at any date after his on-site disappearance. Further investigation is to be undertaken as necessary to calm Rosen down.</p> <p>Known associate of <a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/leveritas-personnel-file">Dr. Veritas</a></p> </div> <img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/david-rosen-file/owlRosen.png" width="32%" alt="owlRosen.png" class="image" /> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p><sup><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><em>肖像素描</em></span></strong></sup></p> <hr /> <p><sup><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">职位：</span></strong></sup><br /> 技术研究员</p> <hr /> <p><sup><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">安保等级：</span></strong></sup><br /> 2级（受限制）</p> <hr /> <p><sup><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">驻地：</span></strong></sup><br /> <em>Site-19</em><br /> <em>Site-██</em></p> <hr /> <p><sup><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">心理档案摘要（2014）：</span></strong></sup><br /> 偏执症<br /> 时盲症</p> <hr /> <p><sup><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">已知关系：</span></strong></sup><br /> Tim Taylor博士（主管）<br /> Blaire Roth博士（精神医师）<br /> Rsr. Patrick Gephart（前辈）<br /> <span style="color: white">Convit特工（折磨者）</span></p> <hr /> <p><sup><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">态度类别：</span></strong></sup><br /> 脾气暴躁</p> <hr /></div> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <p><span style="color: white">David。和你愚蠢的傻样完全不符合的帝王的名字。. A regal name unfit for your crass stupidity.</span></p> <p><span style="color: white">Pat on the back. Kudos. Thinking those silent screams inside your chest that won't stop refusing to stop fearing a dead man's slapping flesh. Consuming everything behind your already-hollow eyes. Emptying your brains for more prying room. We're coming through the rotten gaps in your brittle teeth.</span></p> <p><span style="color: white">Remembering you David? They're hardly thinking about you. Noising inside until you're not thinking about you either. Go ahead.</span></p> <p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size:75%;"><span style="color: white">I open your mouth and <sup>scream</sup></span></span></p> <p><span style="float:left; weight: semibold; margin-left:5px; margin-top:12px; color: black; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 0px 10px;"><br /> 最后编辑于 01:22 PM SCP_ST 由 Doctor Taylor<br /></span></p> <span style="float:right; margin-left:5px; margin-top:12px; color: purple; background-color: #ffffff; padding: 0px 10px;"></span> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /> <span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-2" style="display:none"> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <div class="top-border"></div> <div style="text-align: center;"> <h1><span>故事</span></h1> <hr /></div> <p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span></p> <div class="top-border"></div> <div style="text-align: center;"> <h1><span>其他</span></h1> <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">我突然get到了把作者页当沙盒的好处（？</a></div> </div> </div> <hr /> <div id="wiki-tabview-08b426c200c843f1bf4f9b8154595617" class="yui-navset"> <ul class="yui-nav"> <li class="selected"><a href="javascript:;"><em>一种泥泞的色彩。</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>一点善意的行为。</em></a></li> <li><a href="javascript:;"><em>一千道未愈的伤。</em></a></li> </ul> <div class="yui-content"> <div id="wiki-tab-0-0"> <blockquote> <p>在英语里，我名字的意思是希望。在西班牙语里，它意味着太多的字母。它意味着哀伤，意味着等待。它就像数字九。一种泥泞的色彩。<br /></p> <div style="text-align: right;"> <p>——《芒果街上的小屋》，桑德拉·希斯内罗丝/著，潘帕/译</p> </div> </blockquote> <hr /> <p>这里列出的任何翻译，不管您什么时候看到，有任何的意见或者建议都还请提出来（讨论区或者私信都可以），我看到就会回复。<br /> 有时候我不一定会接受您的意见或者建议，但会附上理由，您也可以选择继续对这份理由进行讨论。<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">其实我很容易被说服的啦</span></p> <hr /> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;SCP文档</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;SCP文档</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;SCP文档</a></div> </div> </div> <hr /> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;故事</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;故事</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;故事</a></div> </div> </div> <hr /> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;GoI格式</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;GoI格式</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;GoI格式</a></div> </div> </div> <hr /> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;艺术作品</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;艺术作品</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;艺术作品</a></div> </div> </div> <hr /> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;作者页</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;作者页</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;作者页</a></div> </div> </div> <hr /> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;其他</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;其他</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;其他</a></div> </div> </div> <hr /> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;我翻译的数量等于这里列出的-2</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;我翻译的数量等于这里列出的-2</a></div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;我翻译的数量等于这里列出的+1</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;我翻译的数量等于这里列出的+1</a></div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;我也不知道是不是中分最受欢迎的翻译作品</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;我也不知道是不是中分最受欢迎的翻译作品</a></div> </div> </div> </div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-1" style="display:none"> <blockquote> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">善良的人：</span></strong> <a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/a-kind-of-christmas">这</a><a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/scp-2331">不是</a>一篇条目。这是一个<a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/the-melody-of-autumn-passing-into-winter">洞</a>，有谁在旅途中<a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/reap-what-you-sew">穿过</a>此处，寻找足够让它们<a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/scp-2772">爱</a>到终结的故事。</p> <p><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/system:page-tags/tag/kindness#pages">它们的脚步还能被感觉到，印入纸页之中。</a><br /></p> <div style="text-align: right;"> <p>——摘自<a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/personnel-and-character-dossier">人员及角色档案</a></p> </div> </blockquote> <p><span style="color: grey">我收集的Kind Man的出场文段。<br /> 感觉现在补完翻译也不必要了全文校对也不必要了，就把它留在这里好了（。</span></p> <p><strong><span style="font-size:larger;">剧透注意。</span></strong></p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;这个折叠页，按一下就是剧透</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;紫色香烟，蓝色墨水</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>按<a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/system:page-tags/tag/kindness#pages">kindness tag</a>顺序排列：</p> <ul> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>A Kind Of Christmas:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">In all instances where the SCP object has been capable of speech, the effector of the breach was described as “a kind man.”</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>From Unknown Admirer to Unknown Admiree:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">Even if it's the kindest of men.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>&#8230;Like Clockwork:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">（其实我看了一遍原文但还是不敢确定）</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>Reap What You Sew:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">On the card, in a neat, blue, cursive script&#8230;The last thing Kairos saw before the lid shut and he was sent off to places unknown, was a loving smile, and a pair of kind eyes.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-1252:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">The letter had no return address and the message contained details of Suzie's condition written in neat blue ink. （蓝色墨水的neat，不过其实不加也可以？）</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-1353:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">I just woke up thinking about some man with kind eyes I saw down the street the day before, how he touched my arm and said he was sorry before walking off.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-1551:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">Especially that man snooping around, the one with the kind smile.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-166:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">（<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">我暂时没找着，</span>不过我喜欢这个故事（。）我找到了！谁能想到会有空白折叠页这种操作啊！</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-1771:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">Upon routine inspection of SCP-1771-03 during fall season, Agent ██ reported finding a letter directed to a non-existent inhabitant referred to only as 'the kind man who did the redecorating'.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-2331:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">I did something very kind for him once. We've had a kind of friendship ever since.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-2353:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">Even that kind, poor fella cashiering the damn place was giving you a side-eye!</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-2442:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">You're kinder than the description frames you, you know.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-2552:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">I AM NO K[illegible].</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-2662:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">Welcome Researcher K███ M██</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-2772:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">On the card was a note written with blue ink in neat cursive containing what is believed to be the entire decoded transcript of Auditory Event 482&#8230;</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-2882:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">'When Kindness Is Eclipsed With Cruelty'（大概是）</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-2909:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">One kind man had put a gun to me.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-2992:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">Doctor K. M██(primary)</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-414:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">Routine interviews will be conducted by Dr. K███ M██.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-5699:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">And even if, you would have still shown me kindness.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-5995:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">（别问，问就是没找着（。（我看了<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">一</span>两遍原文<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">两</span>三遍译文，<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">不过都没有特别仔细，就先这样吧</span>只发现了Agent Kevin McHannon（化名Keith McKinsey）和Kair Malone博士，但我觉得证据不足？？？</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-747:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">Blue crayon written in neat cursive.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-797:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">Dr.K███M██'s note（第二张图每次都把我吓一跳）</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>SCP-979:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">SCP-979 was featured in an exhibition by an artist under the pseudonym of The Kind Man, in the ████████ Museum.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>Seasick Sharks:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">Even the strangers, that kind man who looked to me in pity as if he could know my sacrifice.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>The Melody Of Autumn, Passing Into Winter:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">the scarecrow and his kind friend had their discussion&#8230; His friend was there, sitting in the fog, exhaling a familiar purple smoke.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>The Slow Asphyxiation Of Undiluted Ardor:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">Once, a Kinder person arrived in the lizard's room of love.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>The Special Bond Between Child and Mother:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">even if it is to deliver to a world without Kind Men</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>They Who Find Darkness Loving:</strong></span> <span style="color: white">In that dream a man leans against a white hallway, puffing on a cigarette that produces purple smoke.</span></li> <li><span style="color: #a18cd1"><strong>This Is How We Build Revelation:</strong></span> <span style="color: #1e90ff">The bus driver announced no stops on her way home, kindly silent, and allowed her the space to ponder the difference between migration and abandonment.</span></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <hr /></div> <div id="wiki-tab-0-2" style="display:none"> <div style="text-align: center;"><img src="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/local--files/lyricslinn-s-personnel-file/Avery%20Solace.jpg" style="width: 800px" class="enlarge" alt="Avery%20Solace.jpg" /><br /> <strong><span style="font-size:larger;">是来自<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lyrics-linn" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3935168&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607498379" alt="Lyrics Linn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3935168)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lyrics-linn" >Lyrics Linn</a></span>的<a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/lyricslinn-s-calligraphy-notebook">神仙书法</a>！非常非常感谢(´∀｀)♡</span></strong><br /> <span style="color: grey">虽然我也不知道放在这里是不是特别合适，但既然这个tab就是个安利页就姑且先这样……</span> <hr /> <p><strong>然后也许有人愿意点一下<a href="http://czyesperanza.wikidot.com/all-about-avery-solace">这个链接</a>？</strong></p> </div> <hr /> <blockquote> <p>Avery Solace博士进入它们的房间，换下衣服，假装没有注意到在它们无光的房间中央那儿，那个被漆黑粘液覆盖的人形。</p> <p>该实体只会在心理学家开始爬上床后，才会开始说话。 Lament的声音变得同他腐坏的肉体一样泥泞，在看不见的墙壁间回响着。</p> <p><em>“Avery，今晚又不吃药？你一定喜欢我在你身边吧。真希望其他医生不会嫉妒（get jelly）。”</em><br /> <span style="color: white"><tt>Avery在第二天早餐时才明白这个笑话。</tt></span><br /> “……我没那么糟。不论如何我是他们唯一的测试对象。我不是一只实验老鼠……药物没法让你离开，所以说它不起作用。”</p> <p><em>“好吧，也不能说你不是只小白鼠。”</em><br /> <span style="color: white"><tt>直到它们差点被百吉饼呛住才消停。</tt></span><br /> Solace博士背向声音的来处，试着睡一会。它们最后感觉到的事，是有人在帮他掖被子。<br /></p> <div style="text-align: right;"> <p>——《<a href="http://scp-wiki-cn.wikidot.com/they-who-find-darkness-loving">它们与黑暗相爱</a>》，<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=637830&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607498379" alt="SoullessSingularity" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=637830)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" >SoullessSingularity</a></span>/著，<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gpxx" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4478534&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607498379" alt="GPXx" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4478534)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gpxx" >GPXx</a></span>/译</p> </div> <hr /> <p><span style="color: grey">出于某种原因我也<a href="http://czyesperanza.wikidot.com/they-who-find-darkness-loving">重译</a>了一下这篇，然后明显地发现水平是真的不够啊Orz</span></p> </blockquote> <hr /> <blockquote> <p>Avery Solace盯着ta手里的马尼拉纸质文件夹。被脓液覆盖的Lament特工把他的手臂搭在ta脖子上，越过ta的肩膀看着。自从上一次事故之后，Solace博士第一次感觉到自己被一个团队所需要。“最后的希望”——非常合适的名字。</p> <p>在ta黑暗的房间里，Solace博士换下衣服，躺到床上，盯着天花板。在ta视线的角落，ta的幻觉坐在床边，看着ta试图入睡。</p> <p><em>“又不吃药了，Avery？我真是受宠若惊。”</em>Lament特工的仿制品笑出声来，那声音好像什么柔软又蓬松的东西正在慢慢地死去。</p> <p>Solace博士没有回答。Ta只是不安地沉思着。</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">第一段记忆像一道光芒穿越亿万星辰，</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">在ta的注视下燃烧殆尽。</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>Avery是一个研究小组的一员，该小组负责测试不可转移的认知危害和无害的模因学之间的界限，做的通常是其他不那么秘密的实验室里为实习生准备的工作。这对他认知神经学的博士学位是一种浪费——但又有谁会拒绝研究如此边缘的学科的机会呢？</p> <p>第一次收容失效的时候他正在输入数据。他的导师走了进来，对他大声喊叫——他不记得具体说了什么了。可他永远不会忘记那双眼睛：瞳孔放大，像碧玉环绕着深渊。</p> <p>他记得一阵汹涌的喜悦，像发烧时模糊扭曲的梦。</p> <p>Avery从他的幻梦中清醒过来，发现自己仍被导师凝视着。那双眼睛从他的手掌中盯着他。他不知道她剩余的部分发生了什么。</p> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">第二段记忆从第一段中升起，像胆汁涌上喉咙，</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">不请自来。</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>他负责管理上一次事故后重组的队伍。奇怪的是，一个平凡的科学家组成的小组，怎么竟会像他们研究的异常一样固执。</p> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">最后一段记忆依然疼痛。</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">如一千道未愈合的伤口。</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"></div> </div> </div> <br /> <div style="text-align: right;"> <p>——《<a href="http://scpsandbox2.wikidot.com/soullesshuman">一人血书求作者更新</a><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-641911-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup>》，<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=637830&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607498379" alt="SoullessSingularity" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=637830)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" >SoullessSingularity</a></span>/著，<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/esperanza-cai" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4113182&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607498379" alt="Esperanza_Cai" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4113182)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/esperanza-cai" >Esperanza_Cai</a></span>/译</p> </div> </blockquote> <hr /> <blockquote> <p>“所以……呃，你说啥？”</p> <p>Avery Solace博士并没有明确地在看着Magnus博士。如果ta在看的话，ta就会明白自己刚刚朝他扔了一个重磅炸弹。Ta有特殊的能力可以看穿别人。Magnus博士在一口水喝到一半的时候停下来提出了这个问题。这个时候，两位研究员正在Site 19的餐厅里吃早饭。</p> <p>Solace博士点了点头，动作急促而不稳，更像是肌肉抽搐。“SCP-055。我知道那是什么。大概。”</p> <p>Ta看着Magnus博士抓了抓他的脑袋，一头金发整齐地梳成马尾辫。有几缕头发从束发的皮筋里松脱出来，随即屈服于重力。差不多是早上九点钟，他的发型就已经开始凌乱了。Avery Solace博士也好不到哪里去，穿着一件亟需熨烫的实验服，不过ta从来就没有衣冠齐整过。至少ta今天费心穿上了相配的袜子。</p> <p>Magus博士清了清嗓子。“那。呃。你介意告诉我它是什么吗？”</p> <p>回应他的是一个缓慢、近乎困惑的眨眼。“嗯。”</p> <p>“你是说，你不想告诉我？”</p> <p>又一下急促，僵硬的点头。Solace博士又啜了一口咖啡，快速地瞥了一眼一个空荡的角落，然后轻轻地歪了歪头。Magnus转身顺着ta的视线看过去，什么也没有看到。这让他模糊地想到了自己家里的猫。他转回去看着他的同伴。“那你介意告诉我原因吗？”</p> <p>“……不礼貌？”Avery又歪了歪头，舔了舔干裂的嘴唇，喝了一口咖啡。</p> <p>“你是说你不确定是不是无礼吗？一点都不无礼，Avery。你能——你应该告诉我。现在就说。”较高的那个人的话变得快速、深沉，令人窒息，与其说是请求不如说更像强烈要求。</p> <p>Solace沉默了一段时间。ta呆滞的目光紧张地停留在一个空荡的角落里，眉头皱起，好像被空气冒犯了。“不。我觉得我不会说。人们……人们花了很多心思去搞清楚。他们现在还在努力。我不想毁了他们的乐趣……”</p> <p>有一米八几高的Magnus站了起来，抓住另一位研究员单薄的肩膀。他让ta面对自己。他强迫ta与他对视，目光凌厉，充满了野心与找到突破口的狂热决心。“不，你一定要告诉我。现在就说。”一只手靠近了Solace脆弱的脖子，很容易就能折断。</p> <p>可他的手被小心而坚决地撬开了。Solace拿着他的空盘和咖啡杯站了起来。“……不，那样会很没礼貌。我不想做无礼的事情，Magnus博士。明天见。”</p> <p>要不是会违反人力资源规定，Magnus可能已经揍了ta一顿。<br /></p> <div style="text-align: right;"> <p>——《<a href="http://scpsandbox2.wikidot.com/soulless-sandbox-part-iii">一人血书求作者更新·第二季</a><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-641911-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >2</a></sup>》，<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=637830&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607498379" alt="SoullessSingularity" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=637830)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" >SoullessSingularity</a></span>/著，<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/esperanza-cai" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4113182&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607498379" alt="Esperanza_Cai" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4113182)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/esperanza-cai" >Esperanza_Cai</a></span>/译</p> </div> </blockquote> <hr /> <blockquote> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;迷妹发言已折叠</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;乱七八糟的通感们</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p>【一个半死不活的季节】</p> </div> <p>清冷萧瑟但温暖的秋天。</p> <p>冷。但不是冷酷。温暖。但有时候温暖得很苍白。萧瑟。有点像他经历过又过去了但还会疼的累累伤痕。</p> <p>是那种将尽未尽的秋天，某一个起风的傍晚，本就短命的秋日气数将尽，最后一口气里还吹着干燥了的温暖。</p> <p>即将传入冬日的秋日的旋律。</p> <p>隔着很遥远的时光的距离触碰到的温暖。</p> <hr /> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p>【一种不太好闻的香水】</p> </div> <p>扑面而来的是辛辣的苦味，差不多会让人退避三舍。</p> <p>然后张牙舞爪的气味燃烧殆尽，余烬的味道缠绵不逝，苦味的幽魂仍然缱绻不散地萦绕在背景中，只是没有一开始那么冲的气味，烟雾袅袅。</p> <p>雾色渐深，厚重的木质香气在这个时候一点点漫溢上来，缓慢地温柔地，一点点驱散了余烟呛人的气味，融化了苦涩的棱角，到最后终于只剩一点气味，能让人模糊地回忆起温暖的感受大概会是什么样子。</p> </div> </div> </div> </blockquote> <hr /></div> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/esperanza-cai" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4113182&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607498379" alt="Esperanza_Cai" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4113182)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/esperanza-cai" >Esperanza_Cai</a></span></p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">脚注</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-641911-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. 其实不叫这个名字</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-641911-2"><a href="javascript:;" >2</a>. 同上</div> </div> 
				 	]]>
